# Netlify routing (read from dist/_redirects — works with manual drag-deploy,
# unlike netlify.toml which lives outside dist/).
# "/" serves the pure-static prerendered marketing page (instant paint, no SPA
# boot); "/hotels" serves the prerendered+hydrated Guest Connect marketing page;
# every other path falls through to the SPA (index.html).
#
# esim.mocaintel.com = the public B2C eSIM-compare microsite. Serve the eSIM SPA
# shell (esim.html: same SPA boot as index.html, but with a canonical pointing at
# the apex https://mocaintel.com/esim-deals) for the whole host, so App.jsx
# (IS_ESIM_HOST) renders the compare page at the clean root URL AND the subdomain
# consolidates its SEO signal onto the apex page instead of self-canonicalising.
# MUST precede the "/" landing rule below — first match wins and the path-only
# rules match every host. Non-force (200) so existing static files (assets,
# robots.txt, sitemap.xml) are still served directly on the subdomain.
https://esim.mocaintel.com/*  /esim.html  200
/            /landing.html   200!
/hotels      /hotels.html    200!
# Public consumer eSIM page — served the prerendered esim.html shell so its raw
# HTML carries the correct self-referencing canonical/title/OG (index.html's head
# would point the canonical at the site root and de-index this page).
/esim-deals  /esim.html      200!
# Short branded link for the TikTok bio → the tagged eSIM compare page.
/tt          /esim-deals?utm_source=tiktok&utm_campaign=tiktok_bio   302
/*           /index.html     200
